/-!
# Primes of a local ring of a scheme and points specializing to the point

Let `X` be a scheme, `ξ` a point of `X` and `A = 𝒪_{X, ξ}` the local ring at `ξ`. The canonical
morphism `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.fromSpecStalk` from `Spec A` to `X` is a topological embedding
whose range is the set of points specializing to `ξ`, so it identifies the primes of `A` with the
points of `X` that specialize to `ξ`. This file records what that identification does to an ideal
sheaf: the preimage of the support of `Z` is the zero locus of the stalk of `Z`, and consequently
the minimal primes over the stalk of `Z` at `ξ` are exactly the generic points of the irreducible
components of the support of `Z` passing through `ξ`.

This is the index correspondence the right-hand side of
`Stacks.Chow.length_quotient_span_sup_eq_sum_minimalPrimes_of_notMem_associatedPrimes` is
summed over, and hence the correspondence Stacks Tag 02S5 needs in order to read that identity
as the comparison of `[Z₀]_k` with `∑ nᵢ [(Wᵢ)₀]_k`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Chow.preimage_fromSpecStalk_support_eq_zeroLocus` — the preimage of the support of an
  ideal sheaf `Z` under `X.fromSpecStalk ξ` is the zero locus of the stalk of `Z` at `ξ`.
* `Stacks.Chow.fromSpecStalk_mem_componentGenericPointsThrough_iff` — a prime of `A` is minimal
  over the stalk of `Z` at `ξ` exactly when the corresponding point of `X` is a maximal point of
  the support of `Z`.
* `Stacks.Chow.bijOn_fromSpecStalk_minimalPrimes` — `X.fromSpecStalk ξ` restricts to a bijection
  from the minimal primes over the stalk of `Z` at `ξ` onto the maximal points of the support of
  `Z` specializing to `ξ`.
* `Stacks.Chow.componentGenericPointsThrough_nonempty` — that bijection is between nonempty sets
  whenever `ξ` lies in the support of `Z`.
* `Stacks.Chow.maximal_isIrreducible_closure_of_mem_componentGenericPointsThrough` — a maximal
  point of the support is the generic point of an irreducible component of the support.
* `Stacks.Chow.isLocalization_stalk_of_specializes` — the local ring at a point specializing to
  `ξ` is the localization of `A` at the corresponding prime, the map being
  `TopCat.Presheaf.stalkSpecializes`.
* `Stacks.Chow.idealStalk_eq_map_stalkSpecializes` — the stalk of an ideal sheaf at a point
  specializing to `ξ` is generated by the image of its stalk at `ξ`.
* `Stacks.Chow.length_localizedModule_quotient_idealStalk_eq_length_stalk` and
  `Stacks.Chow.length_localizedModule_quotient_idealStalk_eq_componentMultiplicity` — the length,
  over the localization of `A` at a prime `q`, of the localization of `A ⧸ I` there is the length
  of the local ring of the subscheme of `Z` at the corresponding point, that is, the multiplicity
  of the component through it.
* `Stacks.Chow.idealStalk_vanishingIdeal_closure_fromSpecStalk` — the stalk at `ξ` of the reduced
  closed subscheme supported on the closure of the point corresponding to `q` is `q`.

## Implementation notes

The first statement is read on one affine open `U` containing `ξ`, where `X.fromSpecStalk ξ`
factors as `Spec.map (germ) ≫ hU.fromSpec`: the support of `Z` meets `U` in the zero locus of
the sections `Z.ideal U` (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.coe_support_inter`), the
preimage of that zero locus under `hU.fromSpec` is the prime-spectrum zero locus
(`AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen.fromSpec_preimage_zeroLocus`), and the preimage under
`Spec.map (germ)` turns it into the zero locus of the ideal generated by the image of
`Z.ideal U`, which is the stalk of `Z` at `ξ`.

Maximality of a point of the support is stated without reference to `ξ`: a point `η` of the
support specializing to `ξ` is maximal among the points of the support specializing to `ξ` if
and only if it is maximal among all points of the support, because specialization is transitive.
That is why `Stacks.Chow.componentGenericPointsThrough` imposes its three conditions separately.

The localization statement is the affine computation again: over an affine open `U` containing
`ξ`, both `A` and the local ring at `η` are localizations of `Γ(X, U)`, the second at a smaller
prime, so `IsLocalization.isLocalization_of_submonoid_le` makes the local ring at `η` a
localization of `A` at the image of the smaller prime's complement, and `IsLocalization.of_le`
enlarges that multiplicative set to the whole complement of the prime corresponding to `η`.

The length identity is then three ring isomorphisms away: localizing `A ⧸ I` at `q` is taking
the quotient of `A_q` by the ideal generated by `I`
(`IsLocalizedModule.toLocalizedQuotient'` and `Submodule.localized'_eq_span`), `A_q` is the local
ring at `η`, and the quotient of that by the stalk of `Z` at `η` is the local ring of the
subscheme of `Z`. Only the second of these changes the base ring, and `Module.length R R` is a
ring-isomorphism invariant, which is the private lemma the three steps are glued with.

